<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paknam incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Paknam · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-siamese-war">Franco-Siamese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Paknam incident was a naval clash on 13 July 1893, when two French gunboats forced their way past the Siamese forts at Paknam, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chao-phraya-river">Chao Phraya River</a>, and anchored before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> then blockaded the coast and issued an ultimatum, and by the treaty of October 1893 Siam ceded the territories east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a>, which became part of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paknam-incident.jpg" alt="Paknam incident" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michelet / After Alexandre Jean-Baptiste Brun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%27Illustration_No_2630_22_Juillet_1893_Page_61_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
